    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d64">

                <pb facs="0120" n="854" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg854"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Willis to Mr.
                            Gresham.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Honolulu</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-05-08"><hi rendition="#italic">May 8, 1895</hi></date>.
                        (Received May 1.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 109.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The British Government has just announced
                    its decision as to the citizenship of W. H. Ricard, T. B. Walker, and A. M.
                    Hewett, according to which the first two mentioned, not having voluntarily and
                    knowingly renounced their British citizenship or received certificates of
                    naturalization here, are held to be entitled to the protection of their native
                    country. Mr. Hewett’s claim to British nationality is denied, as he had complied
                    with all the conditions and had accepted a certificate of Hawaiian
                    nationality.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Albert S. Willis.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
